!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
Idioms
description: compositions of the primitives — not new syntax
- 'The everyday questions are compositions of the primitives, never new syntax:'
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Want
    - Query
      width: 3
  - ['members of tag T (the embedded model)', '`T: ?..: ?..: !!<type: binary>` — annotated materials reach the tag forward through their annotations, so members are two uplinks away']
  - ['tags applied to node N', '`: N: yamlover-annotations: [?]: !!<format: x-yamlover-tag>`']
  - ['sub-tags of T (not members)', '`T: ?: !!<*:: yamlover: $defs: tag>`']
  - ['all tag nodes (the tag-picker)', '`:: ...: !!<format: x-yamlover-tag>`']
  - ['find-usages of N', '`N: ?..`']
  - ['every blob under here', '`...: !!<type: binary>`']
- |
  The future extensions — repetition and quantifiers, regex matching, branching, the
  capture sigil, projection — live behind the reserved characters
  (`! ( ) < > = |`), so none of them changes the meaning of a v1 query when it
  lands.
